msgstr "使其余部分成为强制要求而非可有可无的设想"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:251
msgid "Round-trip translation QA"
msgstr "往返翻译 QA"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:251
msgid "Detects drift; a human adjudicates it"
msgstr "检测漂移；由人工进行判定"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:253
msgid "How much of this does Dublin Core carry?"
msgstr "Dublin Core 涵盖了其中的多少？"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:256
msgid "✎ Edit{: .fa-node-edit title=\"Edit content/docs/document-ingestion/how-much-of-this-does-dublin-core-carry.md\" } QA… TR"
msgstr "✎ Edit{: .fa-node-edit title=\"Edit content/docs/document-ingestion/how-much-of-this-does-dublin-core-carry.md\" } QA… TR"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:258
msgid "Some of it, and it is worth being exact about which, because the answer decides whether a field is a  term or something this project invents."
msgstr "涵盖了其中一部分，而明确具体涵盖了哪些很有价值，因为答案决定了一个字段究竟是  术语还是本项目自创的内容。"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:261
msgid "Dublin Core covers the bibliographic layer well — , , , , , , , . The per-folder record and the archive's part/whole structure sit comfortably there."
msgstr "Dublin Core 很好地覆盖了书目层 —— 、、、、、、、。每个文件夹的记录以及归档的部分/整体结构都能很自然地融入其中。"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:265
msgid "It does not cover the derived layer. A narrative description of a figure, a transcript, a back-translation confidence, a sheet's column headers, and above all the provenance of a generated narrative are not  terms, and a published vocabulary is the wrong place to guess an IRI."
msgstr "它并不涵盖衍生层。 图表的叙述性描述、文字记录、回译置信度、工作表的列标题，尤其是所生成叙述的来源溯源，均不是  术语，而在已发布的词汇表中胡乱猜测 IRI 是错误的做法。"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:270
msgid "The house rule already in  decides the shape: generalising is sound; inventing is not. Where an existing vocabulary has the term, use it; where it does not, the term goes in this project's own namespace rather than being bent into an approximate  one. Which vocabularies to reach for first — PROV-O for provenance is the obvious candidate — is not yet decided and must be settled against the published specifications rather than from memory."
msgstr "中既有的内部规则决定了其形态：合理泛化是明智的，凭空捏造则不然。 凡是现有词汇表中已有的术语，直接采用；凡是没有的，该术语应放入本项目自己的命名空间中，而不是被硬套进一个近似的  术语中。优先采用哪些词汇表 —— 用于溯源的 PROV-O 显然是首选候选 —— 目前尚未确定，必须根据已发布的规范而不是凭记忆来定夺。"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:278
msgid "Editing an ingested source"
msgstr "编辑已摄取的来源"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:281
msgid "✎ Edit{: .fa-node-edit title=\"Edit content/docs/document-ingestion/editing-an-ingested-source.md\" } QA… TR"
msgstr "✎ Edit{: .fa-node-edit title=\"Edit content/docs/document-ingestion/editing-an-ingested-source.md\" } QA… TR"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:283
msgid "Ingestion never edits corpus content. It produces L1 records; authoring and review consume them through the ordinary flow in the publication workflow, where a change to a content block goes through validation, findings, and an editor's decision."
msgstr "摄取绝不会编辑语料库内容。它产出 L1 记录；创作和审阅通过发布工作流中的常规流程来消费它们，其中对内容块的修改会经历验证、问题发现以及编辑者的决策。"

#: docs/document-ingestion.md:288
msgid "The one coupling worth stating: a drop into  during an editing session starts ingestion in the background. The editor is not blocked, and the new source becomes citeable when the gate passes — not before."
msgstr "值得说明的一项耦合是：在编辑会话期间向  放入文件会在后台启动摄取。编辑者不会被阻塞，而新来源在关卡通过时即可被引用 —— 绝不会在此之前。"
